What are the benefits and pitfalls of creatinine clearance as a pre-operative diagnostic test?

The benefits of creatinine clearance as a pre-operative diagnostic test include, but are not limited to:

(1) Appropriate renal function can be obtained prior to a procedure that requires a small amount of renal function;

(2) Diagnostic of possible renal insufficiency prior to a procedure can be made (in non-transplant kidney disease cases);

(3) Creatinine clearance can be used to diagnose renal insufficiency in transplant patients if serum creatinine clearance is abnormal;

(4) Creatinine clearance can be used to diagnose renal insufficiency if serum creatinine clearance is abnormal in a patient who is not candidates for transplant.

